        },
        {
          "text": "Gemma3's addition of “format” covers existing RGB conversion, float32 rescaling and channel normalization, followed by channels-first half-precision conversion with a batch dimension. Its fixed-size resize remains unchanged.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_44def8a91944415c86cdca07ac9aea33", "call_c19f541753de44a4b99371ac5c1e5606", "call_863934a8923748ddb391b774048355b1"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mistral3 prepares a square bounding limit from longest_edge and aligns each output dimension to patch_size × spatial_merge_size. This alignment supplies complete patch neighborhoods for merging. It then performs RGB conversion, rescaling, normalization and BCHW half conversion; get_image_embeddings derives the feature grid from the returned size and divides its dimensions by spatial_merge_size for image-token serialization. Grid rounding means aspect-ratio preservation is approximate, not exact.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_6f90181763164b56bc985484e3d8bfa5", "call_5b0ad51112314baea2f8d0827edd2a31", "call_f579319aecdf42ccb0e10d3964b99f3d"]
